}

void processSensorData() {
  // Analyze data and decide actions
}
```

```cpp
// Arduino Sketch

void setup() {
  // Initialize motor pins
  pinMode(MOTOR_PIN, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  // Control motors based on decisions from ESP32
  if (digitalRead(SENSOR_PIN)) {
    digitalWrite(MOTOR_PIN, HIGH); // Move forward
  } else {
    digitalWrite(MOTOR_PIN, LOW); // Stop or reverse direction
  }
}
```

This setup ensures a clear division of tasks between the ESP32 and Arduino. The ESP32 handles communication and complex logic, while the Arduino manages basic motor control. Would you like to add more details or move forward with this?
